  "verbalization": "Zeylanol appears to interact with multiple targets that ultimately lead to the induction of the Induced myeloid leukemia cell differentiation protein Mcl-1. The evidence suggests that Zeylanol acts as a target of several compounds, including 3-O-beta-D-Glucosyl-(1->6)-beta-D-glucosyl-7-O-alpha-L-rhamnosylkaempferol and (-)-Fragransin A2, which in turn target Mcl-1. This indicates that Zeylanol may influence the biological pathways that regulate Mcl-1 expression or activity. The integration of these targets highlights a potential mechanism by which Zeylanol could modulate Mcl-1, possibly through the activation or inhibition of downstream signaling pathways. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting Mcl-1 suggests that Zeylanol may interact with different molecular pathways that converge on this protein, potentially offering a broad therapeutic profile. The evidence supports a role for Zeylanol in the regulation of Mcl-1, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
